commit f227fa0f010d457be49dff4183aff7f9c60bd767
Author:     Daniel Siman Tov <[REDACTED:email]>
AuthorDate: Fri Sep 4 11:37:00 2026 +0300
Commit:     Daniel Siman Tov <[REDACTED:email]>
CommitDate: Fri Sep 4 11:37:00 2026 +0300

    close the six findings from the sixth cold review
    
    Three were slips in the previous round's edit, two were pre-existing product
    holes the smaller diff finally made visible, and one was a CI gap.
    
    - P1 CI was running 102 of 264 tests. unittest.main() sat above classes
      appended later in test_properties.py, and CI invokes that file directly, so
      every regression added in this release was invisible to it. The entry point
      now lives at the end of the file.
    - P1 A self-attested ancestor could become a baseline: a bare
      `--codex pass --glm pass --approve` records a claim that nothing ran, and a
      later L1 change then starts after it, where check schedules no reviewer at
      all. The walk now requires captured evidence — strictly more conservative.
    - P1 A repo could weaken its own test gate. Rewriting test_command to `true` is
      ordinary L1 source by path: no meaningful tests, no review, SAFE TO MERGE.
      Classifying the config FILE as L2 was tried and reverted — it is in the first
      span of every repo after `init`, so it raised the floor fleet-wide on
      adoption. check now compares against the command the last ancestor report ran
      and raises to L2 when it changed. (Reading the baseline's config would never
      fire: rewriting the command invalidates that evidence by construction.)
    - P1 The bare root commit's own files are classified by the floor but were
      excluded from the review packet, so a root-commit migration derived L3 while
      both reviewers read a packet without it.
    - P2 The packet was a corrupt patch: the git wrapper strips the trailing
      newline, so `git apply` refused it. A test now applies the real packet.
    - P2 _validated_baseline returned three values on error paths and two on
      success, so the shallow-history path failed closed by accident, not design.
    
    268 tests via discovery, 142 via the CI entry point, 112 in the gate suite.

